  "id": "COMPOUND:34419 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Notoamide B is implicated in the activation of CX-1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Notoamide B acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Malme-3M, which in turn is a target of other agents such as Methyl 4-Formylbenzoate and Ingenol-20-decanoate. All these compounds ultimately target CX-1, indicating a potential pathway where Notoamide B serves as a bridge in the signaling cascade leading to CX-1 activation. The consistent presence of multiple targets pointing to CX-1 suggests a robust mechanism, possibly involving the modulation of cellular pathways that are downstream of the initial targets. This integrated evidence supports the notion that Notoamide B may influence CX-1 through a network of interconnected molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
